FINAL ANSWER:
# Bus Factor Analysis (all history)

**Project-level bus factor: 2.** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson account for nearly all the meaningful history. Without those two, almost nobody else has touched the core code.

## Overview
The project is tiny: 7 JS files, with the runtime code in one file, `lib/index.js`. I counted commits per file with `git log --follow`. I excluded the "Fiona Formatter" reformat commits from ownership. I didn't run the contributor-analyzer agent, because this repo is small enough to count directly.

| Contributor | Commits | Active period | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 143 | 2017 – Sep 2021 | ❌ Inactive (~5 years) |
| Troy Goode | 95 | 2013 – Apr 2026 | ✅ Active |
| dependabot[bot] | 11 | 2025 – 2026 | bot |
| Everyone else (about 20 people) | 1–4 each | scattered | mostly one-off |

## Single-contributor files
| File | Sole owner | Notes | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| `test/vary.js` | Troy Goode | Only 1 commit, from a recent "vary header coverage" change. | LOW |
| `.eslintrc.yml`, `test/.eslintrc.yml`, `test/support/env.js` | Douglas Wilson | 1 commit each. Config and helpers, and he is inactive. | LOW |
| `.github/dependabot.yml` | Ulises Gascón | 1 commit. | LOW |

## Core files (not strictly single-owner, but concentrated)
| File | Top owners | Dependents | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` (the whole library) | Troy 29 commits, and 138 of ~230 surviving lines (about 60%); Wilson 4 commits | 3 test files | **HIGH** |
| `test/test.js` | Troy 21 commits, Wilson 15 commits | none | MEDIUM |
| `README.md` | Troy 37 of 46 commits (about 80%) | none | MEDIUM |
| `package.json` | Wilson 68, Troy 37 | none | MEDIUM |
| `.github/workflows/*` | Wilson 10 commits on `ci.yml`; the rest is Gascón, Mangas and bots | none | LOW |

## Knowledge heat map
```
repo/
├── lib/            [██████░░░░] 🔴 Bus factor 1–2 (Troy ~60% of surviving lines)
├── test/           [███████░░░] 🟡 Bus factor 2 (Troy + Wilson)
├── .github/        [███░░░░░░░] 🟢 Bus factor 3+ (Wilson, Gascón, Mangas, bots)
├── package.json    [██████░░░░] 🟡 Bus factor 2 (Wilson, Troy)
└── README.md       [████████░░] 🔴 Troy ~80% of commits
```

## Conclusions
- **Troy Goode is the key person.** He is active (last commit April 2026) and is the main author of `lib/index.js`, the tests and the README. If he left, the library would have no active maintainer who knows the core code.
- **Douglas Wilson is a historical dependency.** He has been inactive since 2021, but he is the top owner of `package.json` and `ci.yml` and wrote many of the tests. Most of that knowledge is no longer held by anyone active.
- **Recent contributors are shallow.** Gascón, Church, Beltran and Mangas have 1–3 commits each, mostly CI, dependency and docs work. None has touched the core logic in `lib/index.js`.
- The commit data can't tell me whether the three test files that depend on `lib/index.js` are the only consumers.

## Recommendations
1. **Immediate:** Have a second active contributor review every change to `lib/index.js`, starting with Gascón or Church, who are already active in the repo.
2. **Short-term:** Document the intent of the core handlers in `lib/index.js` and in `test/test.js`. Wilson's knowledge of the tests and release setup is the part most at risk, because he is inactive.
3. **Ongoing:** Rotate PR authorship and review across at least 3 people. Make sure `package.json` and release or CI changes are reviewed by someone other than the author.

