**The bus factor is 2 overall, and 1 if you count only people who are still active.** The person at the center is Troy Goode (<email redacted>).

These numbers come from surviving-lines at 62628c0 (18 files, 315 commits). The activity window ends 2026-04-12, not today.

**Who holds the code** (non-blank lines, then counting blank lines, then commits):

| Author | Non-blank | With blanks | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 605 (36.4%) | 762 (38.4%) | 93 (29.5%) |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 (33.2%) | 629 (31.7%) | 143 (45.4%) |
| Íñigo Marqués Prado (name garbled in the tool output) | 80 (4.8%) | 95 (4.8%) | 2 |
| Jon Church | 59 (3.5%) | 72 (3.6%) | 3 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 (3.4%) | 67 (3.4%) | 2 |
| 40 others | about 310 (about 18.7%) | | |

- **Overall:** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together hold 50% of the lines. Reaching 80% takes 5 people.
- **Active only:** 9 of 44 people committed in the last 365 days, and they hold 51.7% of the lines. Among them the bus factor is 1, Troy Goode. Douglas, the second-largest owner with 33.2%, has no commit in that window. Neither does Íñigo.
- **Identity merge:** Troy appears under two addresses, <email redacted> and troy@laptop.example. If they are the same person, he holds 649 lines (39.0%). This is a guess from names and addresses, and I have not applied it.

**Parts of the codebase that depend on one person:**

| Area | Lines (share of repo) | Top owner (share of that area) |
|---|---|---|
| `lib/` | 214 (12.9%) | Troy Goode, 61.7% |
| `test/` | 820 (49.3%) | Troy Goode, 47.3% |
| `.github/` | 305 (18.4%) | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 30.2% |
| Root files | 323 (19.4%) | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 29.4% |

`lib/` is the core code, and it depends most on Troy. `.github/` and the root files lean on Douglas, who is inactive.

**Files where one person holds 90% or more (at least 20 lines):**
- `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`: Íñigo Marqués Prado, 61 lines. GitHub committed 60 of those lines, but they are credited to Íñigo as the author.
- `.github/workflows/codeql.yml`: Sebastian Beltran, 53 lines.
- `test/vary.js`: Troy Goode, 32 lines.

**Orphaned files:** 6 of 18 files, 7.8% of the lines, have an inactive top owner and no active person holding 20% or more. The largest are `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` (Íñigo, 61 lines), `HISTORY.md` (Douglas, 41) and `LICENSE` (Douglas, 18).

**Other caveats:**
- The latest commit, 62628c0 (the 4-space and double-quote reformat), was set aside. Its lines are credited back to the earlier authors, so it doesn't distort ownership.
- dependabot[bot] is excluded (10 lines, 11 commits).
- The repo history starts with a 2013 import covering 44% of the files, and the table describes work since then.
- The activity window ends 2026-04-12, so anyone who has committed since then isn't reflected. Re-running with a current date would likely show fewer active people.

**Mitigation:** The highest-value step is getting a second active maintainer into `lib/`. The CI workflows should also get an active owner, since they have no one left to maintain them.

